# Constructor payload type precision (Task 10 + I-Case3 interaction fix).
# When matching on a Union type containing NominalVariants with named fields,
# the payload variable receives a Record with the correct field type (Int), not Unknown.
# This verifies the Intersection arm in collect_pattern_bindings:
# arm_scrutinee_ty for multi-arm matches is Intersection([Union([MyOk,MyErr]),
# NominalVariant("MyOk", {n:Int})]) — must search members to find the typed payload.
# If v is Unknown (bug), [+ v 1] would still typecheck (no Addable constraint).
# If v is Record({n: Int}) (correct), p.n is Int and [+ p.n 1] typechecks without error.
[
  Result2: [type [MyOk n: Int] [MyErr msg: Str]]

  # Type-only test: function with typed parameter; we don't call it at runtime.
  # The type checker must see p.n as Int (not Unknown) for [+ p.n 1] to typecheck.
  unwrap-ok: [fn [let r@Result2]
    [match r
      [MyOk p]: [+ p.n 1]
      [MyErr _]: 0
    ]
  ]

  result: 42
]
=== out
Dict({"Result2": Dict({}), "unwrap-ok": Function(r), "result": Int(42)})
